# NrCaches 3

// M2S -> Host-to-Device (H2D)
// S2M -> Device-to-Host (D2H)

// Network:
//
// Primary Memory Protocol: 6 channels (HDM-DB - device coherent with Back-Invalidate (multi-host))
// Note that 6 additionnal channels (mirrored from these ones) exists for direct P2P (type 2 device/accelerators to memory direct).
//
// Assumptions:
// 
// - Device must implement an inclusive snoop filter.
//   i.e., devices maintain top-level directory structure.
//   * p136. device snoop filter can track 2 state or 3 state: I vs A or I/S/A 
//     where A is any state of possible MESI state in the host
//     _ that means CXL.mem technically work as MI or MSI protocol.
//       fine, bc ownership is identical in MESI and MSI, so SWMR isn't affected.
//
// Ordering Rules: (sec. 3.4, p162)
// 
// Upstream:
// - S2M NdR/Drs Cmp-* >>> S2M NdR/Drs BIConflictAck: BIConflictAck must NOT pass prior Cmp* to the same address 
//     _ impl detail p152: tag field from RwD msg must be re-used in BIConflict msg, which is then re-used by the device in Ndr (Cmp or BIConflictAck)
//                         tags are not required to be unique, but fabric enforces strict (fifo?) ordering of similar tags
//                         Note: the tag of the BISnp msg is device initiated, so only BIRsp need to re-use it.
// - S2M NdR/Drs > S2M BISnp: required for deadlock avoidance, i.e., Ndr/Drs must be allowed to pass BISnp to prevent deadlocks
// - other cases: no-ordering requirements.
// Downstream:
// - M2S BIRsp > M2S Req: BIRsp must be allowed to pass Req to prevent deadlocks 
// - M2S BIRsp > M2S RwD: BIRsp must be allowed to pass RwD to prevent deadlocks 
// - M2S RwD > M2S Req: RwD must be allowed to pass Req to prevent deadlocks
// - other cases: no-ordering requirements.
// Summary:
//   * M2S: BIRsp > RwD > Req (priority order)
//   * S2M: NdR/Drs > BISnp (priority order)
//   * S2M: Cmp-* >>> BIConflictAck (fifo ordering required to prevent deadlocks, within NdR channel)
//
// - p.133 "Within a channel, there are no ordering rules, but exceptions to this are described in Section 3.3.11"
// Sec. 3.3.11
//   * BISnp can block Req, but RwD cannot be blocked by BISnp
//       _ I infer that forwarded requests can prevent progress of GetX, but not evict (PutX).
//       * "This rule impacts RwD MemWr* to only use SnpType=No-op (e.g., WB w/o Snoop),
//          The requester must first get ownership using M2S Req message (2-phase write in Sec. 2.4.4)"
//       _ I guess this is just a reminder that it isn't possible to do direct memory writes in Shared FAM HDM-DB,
//         as the BISnp to other sharers could deadlock (everybody blocks
//         on their 1-phase write, that attempt to invalidate other requestors).
//   * Other rules concern ordering relationship of CXL.io and CXL.cache messages with CXL.mem channels.
//   * p135. If outstanding S2M BISnp, then device must block all M2S Req to the same address until S2M BISnp is complete.
//       _ i.e., device must wait for termination of Fwd msg or Inv msg before processing more req.
//       * p136. BISnp due to snoop filter capacity evictions should not block M2S Req, unless snoop filter capacity is actually full
//         i.e., with proper design, M2S Req blocking is rare and not induced by snoop filter capacity limits.
//   * p135. M2S RwD channel must drain without dependence on M2S Req or S2M BISnp
//       _ i.e., hosts must be able to progress on evict/put msg without being blocked by other req or fwd req.
//
// Sec. 3.3.11.1 - Buried Cache State rules
//   - When Req / RwD messages are legal to send, wrt. current buried cache state (state known by host home-agent, e.g., host-side cxl cache).
//
// What is different from MESI?
//
//   - BISnp conflicts:
//     e.g., host receives BiSnpInv but has outstanding request MemRd
//     - host must perform extra handshake with device to clear conflict,
//       either it receives its original response, or an ACK to the conflict message.
//     * case 1: early conflict (p.168):
//       - if host receives BIConflictAck first,
//         it responds with BIRspI to clear up conflict and let the device proceed with original request.
//     * case 2: late conflict (p.168):
//       - if host observes its original response (Cmp-E) before the BIConflictAck,
//         it must process BISnpInv and downgrade itself before responding with BIRspI
//
//   - Block BISnp: CXL defines block commands to BISnp 2 or 4 cache line aligned 128B or 256B blocks
//     * Host home-agent ensures that affected cache lines are all invalid before replying, using its own internal coherence
//     * response is either a single BIRespIBlk for the entire block, or individual BIRspI for each cache line (with idx of CL in the block).
//
//   - Speculative Memory Reads (Sec. 3.5.3.1)
//     host can send MemSpecRd to device to enable reading from memory and resolving coherence in parallel.
//     (specs say that it can help lower latency, but consumes more BW, so not always a good idea in loaded conditions)
//
//   - 
//
// Messages:
//   _ Meta Value:
//     * For Req and RwD, this is the burried cache state (final cache line state in the host)
//       _ I: host is invalid, device can give exclusive ownership as needed
//       _ A: host wants to retain its dirty or exclusive access, device must keep cache line in I state for the in-device caches
//       _ S: host has at most sharable copy, device can share cache line with in-device caches
//     * For Rsp and Drs, this is the cache line state in the dev snoop filter
//   _ SnoopTypes:
//     * SnpData: want at least a shared copy (dev can return exclusive copy also)
//     * SnpCur: want current copy, cannot be cached, no state change
//     * SnpInv: want exclusive copy
//
// *M2S Req
//   -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//   | OpCode        | Meta Value | SnpType | S2M-NdR       | S2M-Drs | Desc                                                          | Equivalent       |
//   -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//   | MemRd         | A          | SnpInv  | Cmp-E         | MemData | Read memory and acquire exclusive ownership                   | GetM             |
//   | MemRd         | S          | SnpData | Cmp-E/S       | MemData | Read memory and acquire sharable copy                         | GetS             |
//   | MemRd         | None       | SnpCur  | Cmp           | MemData | Read current value (uncachable read)                          | ???              |
//   | MemRd         | None       | SnpInv  | Cmp           | MemData | Read current value (uncachable read) & invalidate dev/sharers | ???              |
//   | MemInv        | A          | SnpInv  | Cmp-E         | None    | Acquire ownership without data                                | ???              |
//   | MemInvNT      | A          | SnpInv  | Cmp-E         | None    | Acquire ownership without data & NT (expect writeback soon)   | ???              |
//   | MemInv        | I          | SnpInv  | Cmp           | None    | Invalidate (and flush) other caches (in dev or other hosts)   | ???              |
//   | MemRdData     | None       | SnpData | Cmp-E/S       | MemData | Read memory and acquire S or E copy (ignore meta value)       | ???              |
//   | MemClnEvct    | I          | None    | Cmp           | None    | Host drops E or S copy from its caches (downgrade to I)       | PutX (data-less) |
//   -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// *M2S RwD
//   -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//   | MemWr         | I          | None    | Cmp           | None    | Writeback, do not keep cachable copy                          | WB+PutX          |
//   | MemWr         | A          | None    | Cmp           | None    | Writeback, retain current copy and state                      | WB               |
//   | MemWr         | I          | SnpInv  | Cmp           | None    | Writeback without ownership, Dev must Inv sharers first (illegal in multi-host setting | ??? |
//   | MemWrPtl      | I          | SnpInv  | Cmp           | None    | Same as above, but partial write: contains a mask (dev merge) | ???              |
//   | MemRdFill     | None       | None    | Cmp           | MemData | Read without changing coherence state, useful to merge partial writes in the host | ??? |
//   | BIConflict    | None       | None    | BIConflictAck | None    | Response to BISnp to indicate conflict detected, garbage payload | ???           |
//   -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// *M2S BIRsp
//   -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//   | BIRspI        | N/A        | N/A    | None          | None    | BISnp complete for 1 cache line, Host cache state is I        | ???              |
//   | BIRspS        | N/A        | N/A    | None          | None    | BISnp complete for 1 cache line, Host cache state is S        | ???              |
//   | BIRspE        | N/A        | N/A    | None          | None    | BISnp complete for 1 cache line, Host cache state is E        | ???              |
//   | BIRsp*Blk     | N/A        | N/A    | None          | None    | BISnp complete for X cache lines, Host cache state is (I,S,E) | ???              |
//   -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// *S2M BISnp
//   -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//   | BISnpCur      | N/A       | N/A     |               |         | Dev request current copy but not cachable state               | ???              |
//   | BISnpData     | N/A       | N/A     |               |         | Dev request S cachable copy (returning E is valid)            | Fwd_GetS         |
//   | BISnpInv      | N/A       | N/A     |               |         | Dev request E exclusive cachable copy                         | Fwd_GetM, Inv    |
//   | BISnp*Blk     | N/A       | N/A     |               |         | Same as above, but in Bulk (2, 4 contiguous cache lines)      | ???              |
//   -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// *S2M NdR
//   -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//   | Cmp           | same M2S   | N/A    |               |         | Completion Ack to MemWr, MemRd, MemInv                        | ???              |
//   | Cmp-S         | same M2S   | N/A    |               |         | Completion Ack, Host now has an S copy                        | ???              |
//   | Cmp-E         | same M2S   | N/A    |               |         | Completion Ack, Host now has an E copy                        | ???              |
//   | Cmp-M         | same M2S   | N/A    |               |         | Completion Ack, Host now has an M copy                        | ???              |
//   | BIConflictAck | N/A        | N/A    |               |         | Completion of BIConflict handshake                            | ???              |
//   -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// *S2M Drs
//   -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//   | MemData       | same M2S   | N/A    |               |         | Memory read data                                              | ???              |
//   -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//


Network { 
          Ordered ndr;      // D2H Non-Data-Response (eq. resp PutX_Ack)
          Unordered drs;      // D2H Data-Response (eq. resp GetX_Ack)
          Unordered bisnp;    // D2H Backward-Invalidate-Snoop (eq. fwd Fwd_GetX, Inv)
          Unordered birsp;    // H2D Backward-Invalidate-Response (eq. rsp Inv_Ack, WB)
          Unordered rwd;      // H2D Request-with-Data (eq. req PutX)
          Unordered req;      // H2D Request-without-Data (eq. req GetX)
};

Cache {
    State I;
    Data cl;
    // int[0..NrCaches] acksReceived = 0;
    // int[0..NrCaches] acksExpected = 0;
} set[NrCaches] cache;

Directory {
    State I;
    Data cl;
    set[NrCaches] ID cache;
    ID owner;
} directory;

Message Req{};
Message Rwd{
    Data cl;
};
Message Ndr{};
Message Drs{
    Data cl;
};
Message BISnp{};
Message BIRsp{};


Architecture cache {

    Stable{I, S, E, M}

    // I ////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
    Process(I, load, State){
        msg = Req(MemRd_S_SnpData, ID, directory.ID);
        req.send(msg);

        await{
          when Cmp_S:
            State = S;
            await{
                when MemData:
                    cl=MemData.cl;
                    load;
                    break;
            }

          when Cmp_E:
            State = E;
            await{
                when MemData:
                    cl=MemData.cl;
                    load;
                    break;
            }
        }
    }

    Process(I, load, State){
        msg = Req(MemRdData_SnpData, ID, directory.ID);
        req.send(msg);

        await{
          when Cmp_S:
            State = S;
            await{
                when MemData:
                    cl=MemData.cl;
                    load;
                    break;
            }
        }
    }

    Process(I, store, State){
        msg = Req(MemRd_A_SnpInv, ID, directory.ID);
        req.send(msg);

        await{
          when Cmp_E:
            State = M;
            await{
                when MemData:
                    cl=MemData.cl;
                    store;
                    break;
            }
        }
    }

    // Device ran a BISnp, but we might have received completion of our own conflicting Req/Rwd first due to network re-orderings
    // Simply reply to unblock the device
    Process(I, BISnpData){
        // State is already invalid, just reply
        msg = BIRsp(BIRspI, ID, BISnpData.src);
        birsp.send(msg);
    }

    // Device ran a BISnp, but we might have received completion of our own conflicting Req/Rwd first due to network re-orderings
    // Simply reply to unblock the device
    Process(I, BISnpInv){
        // State is already invalid, just reply
        msg = BIRsp(BIRspI, ID, BISnpInv.src);
        birsp.send(msg);
    }

    // S ////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
    Process(S, load){
        load;
    }

    Process(S, store, State){
        msg = Req(MemInv_A_SnpInv, ID, directory.ID);
        req.send(msg);

        await{
            when Cmp_E:
                store;
                State = M;
                break;
            // TODO check if possible to receive in clean state
            // when BISnpData:
                // Same as BISnpInv, but should go back to S state and reply with BIRspS
            when BISnpInv:
                msg = Rwd(BIConflict, ID, BISnpInv.src);
                rwd.send(msg);

                await{
                    // Completion comes first, we may progress and invalidate after
                    when Cmp_E:
                        // Clean state, no need to wait for MemData here
                        store;
                        State = M;
                        
                        // We cannot just move back to stable M, because BIConflictAck alone doesn't tell us to downgrade to S or I 
                        await{
                            when BIConflictAck:
                                // We are no longer clean, must dirty evict first
                                msg = Rwd(MemWr_I, ID, directory.ID, cl);
                                rwd.send(msg);

                                // Would be nice if we could just move to M_evict_BISnpInv instead - avoid code duplicates
                                await{
                                    when Cmp:
                                        msg = BIRsp(BIRspI, ID, BISnpInv.src);
                                        birsp.send(msg);
                                        State = I;
                                        break;
                                }
                        }

                    // ConflictAck comes first, we may invalidate and wait for completion after
                    when BIConflictAck:
                        // State is clean, no need to run evict message first, can respond directly
                        msg = BIRsp(BIRspI, ID, BISnpInv.src);
                        birsp.send(msg);
                        State = I;

                        await{
                            when Cmp_E:
                                // We are no longer clean, wait for MemData
				await{
				    when MemData:
				        cl=MemData.cl;
                                        store;
                                        State = M;
				        break;
			        }
                        }
                }
        }
    }

    Process(S, evict, State){
        msg = Req(MemClnEvct_I, ID, directory.ID);
        req.send(msg);

        await{
            when Cmp:
                State = I;
                break;
            // when BISnpInv:
            // Specs tell us that BIConflict should always be used, but really doesn't seem useful here
            //     Let's not do anything here, transient state should be generated fine for BISnpInv
            // No channel ordering between Req (MemClnEvict) and BISnp, or between BIRsp and Ndr/Drs
            // Technically, we need to run BIConflict (as per spec requirements) - but here, seems that strict ordering doesn't really matter between those 2 requests
            //     Clean state, so action for both: downgrade to I and reply back
            // In conclusion, do not do anything here, simply make sure that the 2 requests are no blocking each other
            //     (progress should happen with interleaved messages)
            // However, this means that we could receive BISnp message although we are already back to I stable state.
        }
    }

    // Device wants an uncachable current copy of cache line
    // We omit it for now, since directory will never use it
    // TODO: double check if possible to receive in a Clean state
    // Process(S, BISnpCur){
    //    msg = Rwd(MemWr_S, ID, BISnpCur.src, cl);
    //    rwd.send(msg);
    //
    //    await{
    //        when Cmp:
    //            msg = BIRsp(BIRspS, ID, BISnpCur.src);
    //            birsp.send(msg);
    //            break;
    //    }
    // }

    // Device wants a shared copy of cache line
    // TODO: double check if possible to receive in a Clean state
    Process(S, BISnpData){
        // msg = Rwd(MemWr_S, ID, BISnpData.src, cl);
        // rwd.send(msg);

        // await{
        //     when Cmp:
        //        msg = BIRsp(BIRspS, ID, BISnpData.src);
        //        birsp.send(msg);
        //        break;
        // }

        // State is clean, just reply
        msg = BIRsp(BIRspS, ID, BISnpData.src);
        birsp.send(msg);
    }

    // Device wants exclusive copy of cache line
    Process(S, BISnpInv, I){
        // State is clean, just reply
        msg = BIRsp(BIRspI, ID, BISnpInv.src);
        birsp.send(msg);
    }


    // M ////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
    Process(M, load){
        load;
    }

    Process(M, store){
        store;
    }

    Process(M, evict, State){
        msg = Rwd(MemWr_I, ID, directory.ID, cl);
        rwd.send(msg);

        await{
            when Cmp:
                State = I;
                break;

            // Normally, all Req should respond with BIConflict to BISnp when received before Req Completion message
            // - However, we already sent data, and BISnp cannot block RwD at the device, so no need to run BIConflict to check serialization order
            //   i.e., If BISnp is received first, then wait for Cmp, and respond with BIRspI afterwards.
            //         If Cmp is received first, BIConflict won't change anything. BISnp should be handled from new stable state.
            // when BISnpCur:
            //    await{
            //        when Cmp:
            //            msg = BIRsp(BIRspI, ID, BISnpCur.src);
            //            birsp.send(msg);
            //            State = I;
            //            break;
            //    }
            when BISnpData:
                await{
                    when Cmp:
                        msg = BIRsp(BIRspI, ID, BISnpData.src);
                        birsp.send(msg);
                        State = I;
                        break;
                }
            when BISnpInv:
                await{
                    when Cmp:
                        msg = BIRsp(BIRspI, ID, BISnpInv.src);
                        birsp.send(msg);
                        State = I;
                        break;
                }
        }
    }

    // Device wants an uncachable current copy of cache line
    // We omit it for now, since directory will never use it
    // Process(M, BISnpCur){
    //    msg = Rwd(MemWr_A, ID, BISnpCur.src, cl);
    //    rwd.send(msg);

    //    await{
    //        when Cmp:
    //            msg = BIRsp(BIRspE, ID, BISnpCur.src);
    //            birsp.send(msg);
    //            break;
    //    }
    // }

    // Device wants a shared copy of cache line
    Process(M, BISnpData, State){
        msg = Rwd(MemWr_S, ID, BISnpData.src, cl);
        rwd.send(msg);

        await{
            when Cmp:
                msg = BIRsp(BIRspS, ID, BISnpData.src);
                birsp.send(msg);
                State = S;
                break;
        }
    }

    // Device wants exclusive copy of cache line
    Process(M, BISnpInv, State){
        msg = Rwd(MemWr_I, ID, BISnpInv.src, cl);
        rwd.send(msg);

        await{
            when Cmp:
                msg = BIRsp(BIRspI, ID, BISnpInv.src);
                birsp.send(msg);
                State = I;
                break;
        }
    }

    // E ////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
    Process(E, load){
        load;
    }

    Process(E, store, M){
        store;
    }

    Process(E, evict, State){
        msg = Req(MemClnEvct_I, ID, directory.ID);
        req.send(msg);

        await{
            when Cmp:
                State = I;
                break;
            // No channel ordering between Req (MemClnEvict) and BISnp, or between BIRsp and Ndr/Drs
            // Technically, we need to run BIConflict (as per spec requirements) - but here, seems that strict ordering doesn't really matter between those 2 requests
            //     Clean state, so action for both: downgrade to I and reply back
            // In conclusion, do not do anything here, simply make sure that the 2 requests are no blocking each other
            //     (progress should happen with interleaved messages)
        }
    }

    // Device wants an uncachable current copy of cache line
    // We omit it for now, since directory will never use it
    // TODO: check if possible to receive in a Clean state
    // Process(E, BISnpCur){
    //    msg = Rwd(MemWr_A, ID, BISnpCur.src, cl);
    //    rwd.send(msg);
    //
    //    await{
    //        when Cmp:
    //            msg = BIRsp(BIRspE, ID, BISnpCur.src);
    //            birsp.send(msg);
    //            break;
    //    }
    // }

    // Device wants a shared copy of cache line
    Process(E, BISnpData, S){
        // State is clean, just reply
        msg = BIRsp(BIRspS, ID, BISnpData.src);
        birsp.send(msg);
    }

    // Device wants exclusive copy of cache line
    Process(E, BISnpInv, I){
        // TODO check if we can actually skip the CL writeback
        // msg = Rwd(MemWr_I, ID, BISnpInv.src, cl);
        // rwd.send(msg);

        // await{
        //    when Cmp:
        //       msg = BIRsp(BIRspI, ID, BISnpInv.src);
        //       birsp.send(msg);
        //       State = I;
        //       break;
        // }
        
        // State is clean, just reply
        msg = BIRsp(BIRspI, ID, BISnpInv.src);
        birsp.send(msg);
    }

}


Architecture directory {

    Stable{I, S, E, M}

    // I ////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
    Process(I, MemRd_S_SnpData, S){
       // Responding with Cmp_E is also valid, but discouraged since S was resquested (specs say so ...)
       msg = Ndr(Cmp_S, ID, MemRd_S_SnpData.src);
       ndr.send(msg);
       msg = Drs(MemData, ID, MemRd_S_SnpData.src, cl);
       drs.send(msg);
       //owner = MemRd_S_SnpData.src;
       cache.add(MemRd_S_SnpData.src);
    }
    
    // Not used currently in Cache specs
    Process(I, MemRdData_SnpData, E){
       // No meta value specified, respond with E
       msg = Ndr(Cmp_E, ID, MemRdData_SnpData.src);
       ndr.send(msg);
       msg = Drs(MemData, ID, MemRdData_SnpData.src, cl);
       drs.send(msg);
       owner = MemRdData_SnpData.src;
    }

    Process(I, MemRd_A_SnpInv, M){
       msg = Ndr(Cmp_E, ID, MemRd_A_SnpInv.src);
       ndr.send(msg);
       msg = Drs(MemData, ID, MemRd_A_SnpInv.src, cl);
       drs.send(msg);
       owner = MemRd_A_SnpInv.src;
    }

    // S ////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
    Process(S, MemRd_S_SnpData){
       msg = Ndr(Cmp_S, ID, MemRd_S_SnpData.src);
       ndr.send(msg);
       msg = Drs(MemData, ID, MemRd_S_SnpData.src, cl);
       drs.send(msg);
       cache.add(MemRd_S_SnpData.src);
    }
    
    // Not used currently in Cache specs
    Process(S, MemRdData_SnpData){
       // No meta value specified, respond with S
       msg = Ndr(Cmp_S, ID, MemRdData_SnpData.src);
       ndr.send(msg);
       msg = Drs(MemData, ID, MemRdData_SnpData.src, cl);
       drs.send(msg);
       cache.add(MemRdData_SnpData.src);
    }

    Process(S, MemRd_A_SnpInv){
       // 1- If is in the sharer list, remove from sharer list
       // 2- Invalidate all sharers, and wait for reply
       //   - Only clean sharers, so can receive MemClnEvct or BIRspI, all should be in the await block (messages shouldn't block each other)
       // 3- Once all are invalidated, reply back to requestor

       // Requestor shouldn't be a sharer, since he requested the Data, but this cannot hurt
       if cache.contains(MemRd_A_SnpInv.src){
           cache.del(MemRd_A_SnpInv.src);
       }

       msg = BISnp(BISnpInv, ID, ID);
       bisnp.mcast(msg, cache);
       await{
           when BIRspI:
                cache.del(BIRspI.src);
                
                // Once all are invalidated, reply to requestor with perm and data
                if cache.count() == 0{
                    msg = Ndr(Cmp_E, ID, MemRd_A_SnpInv.src);
                    ndr.send(msg);
                    msg = Drs(MemData, ID, MemRd_A_SnpInv.src, cl);
                    drs.send(msg);
                    // Finally, update internal state
                    owner = MemRd_A_SnpInv.src;
                    cache.clear();
                    State=M;
                    break;
                }

           when MemClnEvct_I:
                // Respond but wait for BIRspI to remove from sharers (otherwise we may concluse BISnp flow while some BIRsp are still in flight)
                msg = Ndr(Cmp, ID, MemClnEvct_I.src);
                ndr.send(msg);
                // cache.del(MemClnEvct_I.src);

           // Other caches may have MemRd_A_SnpInv in-flight
           when BIConflict:
                // Host had outstanding Req for that cache line,
                // reply with ACK and wait for their BIRspI
                msg = Ndr(BIConflictAck, ID, BIConflict.src);
                ndr.send(msg);
        }

    }

    Process(S, MemInv_A_SnpInv){
       // 1- Should be in the sharer list, remove from sharer list
       // 2- Invalidate all sharers, and wait for reply
       //   - Only clean sharers, so can receive MemClnEvct or BIRspI, all should be in the await block (messages shouldn't block each other)
       // 3- Once all are invalidated, reply back to requestor

       // Requestor shouldn't be a sharer, since he requested the Data, but this cannot hurt
       if cache.contains(MemInv_A_SnpInv.src){
           cache.del(MemInv_A_SnpInv.src);
       }

       msg = BISnp(BISnpInv, ID, ID);
       bisnp.mcast(msg, cache);
       await{
           when BIRspI:
                cache.del(BIRspI.src);
                
                // Once all are invalidated, reply to requestor with perm and data
                if cache.count() == 0{
                    msg = Ndr(Cmp_E, ID, MemInv_A_SnpInv.src);
                    ndr.send(msg);
                    // Requestor didn't ask for data
                    // msg = Drs(MemData, ID, MemInv_A_SnpInv.src, cl);
                    // drs.send(msg);
                    // Finally, update internal state
                    owner = MemInv_A_SnpInv.src;
                    cache.clear();
                    State=M;
                    break;
                }

           when MemClnEvct_I:
                // Respond but wait for BIRspI to remove from sharers (otherwise we may concluse BISnp flow while some BIRsp are still in flight)
                msg = Ndr(Cmp, ID, MemClnEvct_I.src);
                ndr.send(msg);
                // cache.del(MemClnEvct_I.src);

           // Other caches may have MemRd_A_SnpInv in-flight
           when BIConflict:
                // Host had outstanding Req for that cache line,
                // reply with ACK and wait for their BIRspI
                msg = Ndr(BIConflictAck, ID, BIConflict.src);
                ndr.send(msg);
        }

    }

    Process(S, MemClnEvct_I){
       msg = Ndr(Cmp, ID, MemClnEvct_I.src);
       ndr.send(msg);
       cache.del(MemClnEvct_I.src);

       if cache.count() == 0{
            State=I;
            break;
       }
    }

    // M ////////////////////////////////////////////////////////

    // Host wants S sharable copy
    Process(M, MemRd_S_SnpData){
       // 1- Invalidate owner and wait for MemWr
       //   - May be dirty, so can receive MemWr_I or MemClnEvct_I before BIRspI
       //   - If dirty, host will wait for Cmp before replying with BIRspI, so ordering isn't an issue
       // 3- Once invalidated, reply back to requestor
       
       msg = BISnp(BISnpData, ID, owner);
       bisnp.send(msg);

       await{
           when BIRspS:
               // Completion
               undefine owner;
               cache.add(BIRspS.src);
               cache.add(MemRd_S_SnpData.src);

               msg = Ndr(Cmp_S, ID, MemRd_S_SnpData.src);
               ndr.send(msg);
               msg = Drs(MemData, ID, MemRd_S_SnpData.src, cl);
               drs.send(msg);
               
               State=S;
               break;

           when BIRspI:
               // Completion
               cache.del(BIRspI.src);
               undefine owner;

               msg = Ndr(Cmp_S, ID, MemRd_S_SnpData.src);
               ndr.send(msg);
               msg = Drs(MemData, ID, MemRd_S_SnpData.src, cl);
               drs.send(msg);

               cache.add(MemRd_S_SnpData.src);
               State=S;
               break;

           when MemClnEvct_I:
                // (Self eviction clean), simply respond and wait for completion message
                msg = Ndr(Cmp, ID, MemClnEvct_I.src);
                ndr.send(msg);

           when MemWr_S:
                // Owner was dirty, WB and respond and wait for completion message
                msg = Ndr(Cmp, ID, MemWr_S.src);
                ndr.send(msg);
                if MemWr_S.src == owner{
                    cl = MemWr_S.cl;
                }
           
           when MemWr_I:
                // Owner was dirty, WB and respond and wait for completion message
                msg = Ndr(Cmp, ID, MemWr_I.src);
                ndr.send(msg);
                if MemWr_I.src == owner{
                    cl = MemWr_I.cl;
                }
           
           // Other caches may have MemRd_A_SnpInv in-flight
           when BIConflict:
                // Host had outstanding Req for that cache line,
                // reply with ACK and wait for their BIRspI
                msg = Ndr(BIConflictAck, ID, BIConflict.src);
                ndr.send(msg);
       }

    }
    
    // Host wants E/M exclusive copy
    Process(M, MemRd_A_SnpInv){
       // 1- Invalidate owner and wait for MemWr
       //   - May be dirty, so can receive MemWr_I or MemClnEvct_I and then BIRspI
       //   - If dirty, host will wait for Cmp before replying with BIRspI, so ordering isn't an issue
       // 3- Once invalidated, reply back to requestor
       
       msg = BISnp(BISnpInv, ID, owner);
       bisnp.send(msg);

       await{
           when BIRspI:
               // Completion
               cache.del(BIRspI.src);
               undefine owner;

               msg = Ndr(Cmp_E, ID, MemRd_A_SnpInv.src);
               ndr.send(msg);
               msg = Drs(MemData, ID, MemRd_A_SnpInv.src, cl);
               drs.send(msg);

               owner = MemRd_A_SnpInv.src;
               cache.clear();
               State=M;
               break;

           when MemClnEvct_I:
                // (Self eviction clean), simply respond and wait for completion message
                msg = Ndr(Cmp, ID, MemClnEvct_I.src);
                ndr.send(msg);

           when MemWr_I:
                // Owner was dirty, WB and respond and wait for completion message
                msg = Ndr(Cmp, ID, MemWr_I.src);
                ndr.send(msg);
                if MemWr_I.src == owner{
                    cl = MemWr_I.cl;
                }
           
           // Other caches may have MemRd_A_SnpInv in-flight
           when BIConflict:
                // Host had outstanding Req for that cache line,
                // reply with ACK and wait for their BIRspI
                msg = Ndr(BIConflictAck, ID, BIConflict.src);
                ndr.send(msg);
       }

    }

    // Host wants to WB and drop its copy
    Process(M, MemWr_I){
       msg = Ndr(Cmp, ID, MemWr_I.src);
       ndr.send(msg);
       cache.del(MemWr_I.src);

       if owner == MemWr_I.src{
            cl = MemWr_I.cl;
            undefine owner;
            State=I;
       }
    }

    // Host wants to WB but retain sharable copy
    Process(M, MemWr_S){
       msg = Ndr(Cmp, ID, MemWr_S.src);
       ndr.send(msg);

       if owner == MemWr_S.src{
            cl = MemWr_S.cl;
            undefine owner;
            State=S;
       }
    }

    // Host wants to drop its Clean copy
    Process(M, MemClnEvct_I){
       msg = Ndr(Cmp, ID, MemClnEvct_I.src);
       ndr.send(msg);
       cache.del(MemClnEvct_I.src);

       if owner == MemClnEvct_I.src{
            undefine owner;
            State=I;
       }
    }

    // E ////////////////////////////////////////////////////////

    // Host wants S sharable copy
    Process(E, MemRd_S_SnpData){
       // 1- Invalidate owner and wait for MemWr
       //   - May be dirty, so can receive MemWr_I or MemClnEvct_I before BIRspI
       //   - If dirty, host will wait for Cmp before replying with BIRspI, so ordering isn't an issue
       // 3- Once invalidated, reply back to requestor
       
       msg = BISnp(BISnpData, ID, owner);
       bisnp.send(msg);

       await{
           when BIRspS:
               // Completion
               undefine owner;
               cache.add(BIRspS.src);
               cache.add(MemRd_S_SnpData.src);

               msg = Ndr(Cmp_S, ID, MemRd_S_SnpData.src);
               ndr.send(msg);
               msg = Drs(MemData, ID, MemRd_S_SnpData.src, cl);
               drs.send(msg);
               
               State=S;
               break;

           when BIRspI:
               // Completion
               undefine owner;
               cache.del(BIRspI.src);
               cache.add(MemRd_S_SnpData.src);

               msg = Ndr(Cmp_S, ID, MemRd_S_SnpData.src);
               ndr.send(msg);
               msg = Drs(MemData, ID, MemRd_S_SnpData.src, cl);
               drs.send(msg);

               State=S;
               break;

           when MemClnEvct_I:
                // (Self eviction clean), simply respond and wait for completion message
                msg = Ndr(Cmp, ID, MemClnEvct_I.src);
                ndr.send(msg);

           when MemWr_S:
                // Owner was dirty, WB and respond and wait for completion message
                msg = Ndr(Cmp, ID, MemWr_S.src);
                ndr.send(msg);
                if MemWr_S.src == owner{
                    cl = MemWr_S.cl;
                }
           
           when MemWr_I:
                // Owner was dirty, WB and respond and wait for completion message
                msg = Ndr(Cmp, ID, MemWr_I.src);
                ndr.send(msg);
                if MemWr_I.src == owner{
                    cl = MemWr_I.cl;
                }
           
           // Other caches may have MemRd_A_SnpInv in-flight
           when BIConflict:
                // Host had outstanding Req for that cache line,
                // reply with ACK and wait for their BIRspI
                msg = Ndr(BIConflictAck, ID, BIConflict.src);
                ndr.send(msg);
       }

    }
 
    // Host wants E/M exclusive copy
    Process(E, MemRd_A_SnpInv){
       // 1- Invalidate owner and wait for MemWr
       //   - May be dirty, so can receive MemWr_I or MemClnEvct_I and then BIRspI
       //   - If dirty, host will wait for Cmp before replying with BIRspI, so ordering isn't an issue
       // 3- Once invalidated, reply back to requestor
       
       msg = BISnp(BISnpInv, ID, owner);
       bisnp.send(msg);

       await{
           when BIRspI:
               // Completion
               // Host can only send Req/RwD, or respond to BISnp.
               // If Req/RwD are received first, Host will wait for completion before responding to BISnp
               // In all, BIResp can only be received last, even with unordered network.
               // TODO: check if we are not more restrictive than specs for blocked Req/RwD here
               cache.del(BIRspI.src);
               undefine owner;

               msg = Ndr(Cmp_E, ID, MemRd_A_SnpInv.src);
               ndr.send(msg);
               msg = Drs(MemData, ID, MemRd_A_SnpInv.src, cl);
               drs.send(msg);

               owner = MemRd_A_SnpInv.src;
               cache.clear();
               State=M;
               break;

           when MemClnEvct_I:
                // (Self eviction clean), simply respond and wait for completion message
                msg = Ndr(Cmp, ID, MemClnEvct_I.src);
                ndr.send(msg);

           when MemWr_I:
                // Owner was dirty, WB and respond and wait for completion message
                msg = Ndr(Cmp, ID, MemWr_I.src);
                ndr.send(msg);
                if MemWr_I.src == owner{
                    cl = MemWr_I.cl;
                }
           
           // Other caches may have MemRd_A_SnpInv in-flight
           when BIConflict:
                // Host had outstanding Req for that cache line,
                // reply with ACK and wait for their BIRspI
                msg = Ndr(BIConflictAck, ID, BIConflict.src);
                ndr.send(msg);
       }

    }

    // Host wants to WB and drop its copy
    Process(E, MemWr_I){
       msg = Ndr(Cmp, ID, MemWr_I.src);
       ndr.send(msg);
       cache.del(MemWr_I.src);

       if owner == MemWr_I.src{
            cl = MemWr_I.cl;
            undefine owner;
            State=I;
       }
    }

    // Host wants to WB but retain sharable copy
    Process(E, MemWr_S){
       msg = Ndr(Cmp, ID, MemWr_S.src);
       ndr.send(msg);

       if owner == MemWr_S.src{
            cl = MemWr_S.cl;
            undefine owner;
            cache.add(MemWr_S.src);
            State=S;
       }
    }

    // Host wants to drop its Clean copy
    Process(E, MemClnEvct_I){
       msg = Ndr(Cmp, ID, MemClnEvct_I.src);
       ndr.send(msg);
       cache.del(MemClnEvct_I.src);

       if owner == MemClnEvct_I.src{
            undefine owner;
            State=I;
       }
    }

}
